{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Therefore</b>: Rabbi Moses said: הלום is from the root of והלמה סיסרא, as if it were written הלום with a kamatz in the heh and shureq in the vav, like מוכה and נגוע." "<b>And who is filled</b>: כוס is defective [in vocalization]." "<b>They find</b>: from the root ומצית, and the word came as a mil'el, because the accent is at the beginning of the word, for this is the rule of the language, like: עשה לי את החיל הזה." "<b>The mem of למו</b>: it refers back to those mentioned at the beginning of the psalm, who are ברי לבב. And the correct interpretation: it refers to the word עמו, for it is found both in singular and plural. And in my opinion: הלום is like הנה, as in הבא עד הלום איש, for עמו ישוב — on account of this that he sees; or ישוב from the root שובב, or he brings back to his heart. And I do not know what the reason for this is."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 73, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:13.105848342Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}